DISPOSITION of the 2 hash mismatches (rows 41, 42):
  11.fuzz_aes_gcm and 11.fuzz_ed25519 are the FIRST TWO TARGETS of the
  in-flight item-11 re-soak launched this session.  fuzz_soak.sh writes each
  target's log to logs/item11-<target>.log, so those two files are being
  rewritten right now by the running 2 h jobs (PIDs 6812, 6813).  The stored
  hashes belong to the earlier interrupted (exit 137) runs, whose rows those
  are.  When each re-soak finishes, the driver appends a NEW row with the new
  log's hash, superseding the interrupted row.
  This is a live-rewrite condition, NOT a tampered or lost log.  It is recorded
  as a genuine exit-1 rather than excluded from the criterion, and a final
  re-verification must be run once the long jobs are complete.

STANDING RULE ESTABLISHED BY THIS GAP:
  a run whose log path collides with a previously-hashed log invalidates that
  hash.  Re-soaks must therefore be re-verified at the end of the session, and
  this check is the gate that catches it.
